  "summary_en": "New Zealand's Civil Aviation Act 2023 (consolidated as at 23 October 2026) is the comprehensive aviation statute. It covers participants, the CAA and Director, rules, aviation documents, security, international aviation, airports, carriage liability, and enforcement. It includes powers to seize or destroy aircraft without a person on board (e.g., drones), but has no AI-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establishes CAA, Director of Civil Aviation and Minister's rule-making powers for aviation safety and security",
   "Aviation documents, fit-and-proper-person test, medical certification and drug/alcohol testing",
   "Sections 316-321 allow seizing, detaining or destroying aircraft without a person on board",
   "Duty to notify accidents and incidents, with protection for safety information",
   "Repeals Civil Aviation Act 1990 and Airport Authorities Act 1966"
